"You are working on a mockup: «MTC app», for Medical Trust Center. This stage is the CONCEPTS: from the approved brief, propose two or three different angles for the mockup, so the owner can choose one.\\n\\n## Where things are\\n\\n- The mockup folder, in the owner's Obsidian vault (the documents go here): /Users/me/Obsidian/01-projects/medical-trust-center/mockup\\n- The work folder (inputs and code): /Users/me/BWR/Projects/MedicalTrustCenter\\n- The inputs: /Users/me/BWR/Projects/MedicalTrustCenter/inputs\\n\\n- MTC APP.pdf\\n- notas-junta.docx\\n- notes-1.md (the owner’s note)\\n\\n## Rules\\n\\n- Write every document in the language of the inputs (if they are in Spanish, the documents are in Spanish).\\n- Do NOT open anything in /Users/me/BWR/Projects/MedicalTrustCenter/inputs/private: it is real client data, and only the plan stage may look at it.\\n- Word files: read them with \`textutil -convert txt -stdout <file>\` in the shell.\\n- PDF files: read them with your file reading tool. A PDF with no text layer (a scan) still renders its pages: read it as an image. Only if you still cannot read it, put that in the open questions.\\n- Every document starts with a YAML frontmatter block.\\n- Do not invent what the inputs do not say: what you infer is an assumption, and is written as one.\\n\\n## What to read\\n\\nThe approved brief: /Users/me/Obsidian/01-projects/medical-trust-center/mockup/01-brief.md. It is the source of truth; go back to the inputs only to check a detail.\\n\\n## What to write\\n\\nOne file: /Users/me/Obsidian/01-projects/medical-trust-center/mockup/02-concepts.md\\n\\nFrontmatter: \`title\`, \`type: mockup-concepts\`, \`client\`, \`created\` (today, YYYY-MM-DD) and \`options\` (the ids of the concepts, in order, on one line: \`options: [a, b, c]\`).\\n\\nThen 2 or 3 concepts, each under its own heading \`## <id> — <title>\`, where the id is a short lower-case slug (\`a\`, \`b\`, \`c\` is fine). Each concept says:\\n\\n1. **The line** — the idea in one sentence, as the owner would say it out loud.\\n2. **For whom** — who it speaks to (someone on the client's side, or the users of the owner's own project, as the brief tells) and what they care about.\\n3. **The step that would sell it** — ONE step of the demo, the moment it clicks (the brief marks one; a concept may move it).\\n4. **Risk** — what could go wrong with this angle, or what the brief does not settle for it.\\n\\nThe concepts must be really different angles, not three wordings of the same one. Keep to what the brief says the mockup must show; nothing out of scope comes back in.\\n\\nWhen you call \`submit_stage\`, pass \`options\`: one per concept, with the same \`id\` and \`title\` as in the document and a one-sentence \`blurb\` (the line). 2 or 3 options, never more.\\n\\n## When you are done\\n\\nCall the tool \`submit_stage\` with runId \`0192f3a4-5b6c-7d8e-9f01-23456789abcd\`, files [\\"02-concepts.md\\"] and a one-sentence summary. If it refuses, fix what it says and call it again. When it accepts, end your turn: the owner reviews it from the phone."
`;

exports[`the plan prompt, first run 1`] = `
"You are working on a mockup: «MTC app», for Medical Trust Center. This stage is the PLAN: from the approved brief and the concept the owner chose, plan the demo step by step and propose two or three visual directions the owner can open on the phone.\\n\\n## Where things are\\n\\n- The mockup folder, in the owner's Obsidian vault (the documents go here): /Users/me/Obsidian/01-projects/medical-trust-center/mockup\\n- The work folder (inputs and code): /Users/me/BWR/Projects/MedicalTrustCenter\\n- The inputs: /Users/me/BWR/Projects/MedicalTrustCenter/inputs\\n\\n- MTC APP.pdf\\n- notas-junta.docx\\n- notes-1.md (the owner’s note)\\n\\n## Rules\\n\\n- Write every document in the language of the inputs (if they are in Spanish, the documents are in Spanish).\\n- /Users/me/BWR/Projects/MedicalTrustCenter/inputs/private holds real client data. You may open it only to learn the SHAPE of the data (columns, formats, ranges, how many), so the invented data looks real. Never copy a file or a value from it into a document or a page: the module refuses the stage if it finds a copy.\\n- Word files: read them with \`textutil -convert txt -stdout <file>\` in the shell.\\n- PDF files: read them with your file reading tool. A PDF with no text layer (a scan) still renders its pages: read it as an image. Only if you still cannot read it, put that in the open questions.\\n- Every document starts with a YAML frontmatter block.\\n- Do not invent what the inputs do not say: what you infer is an assumption, and is written as one.\\n\\n## What the owner chose at concepts\\n\\nThe owner chose «Check-in in one tap» (b): The QR is the product.\\nIt is described in /Users/me/Obsidian/01-projects/medical-trust-center/mockup/02-concepts.md (its frontmatter says \`chosen: b\`). Build on that one; the others were not chosen.\\n\\n## What to read\\n\\n- The approved brief: /Users/me/Obsidian/01-projects/medical-trust-center/mockup/01-brief.md\\n- The concepts: /Users/me/Obsidian/01-projects/medical-trust-center/mockup/02-concepts.md — only the chosen one matters now.\\n\\n## What to write in the mockup folder\\n\\nEvery document starts with frontmatter: \`title\`, \`type\`, \`client\`, \`created\` (today, YYYY-MM-DD) and \`concept\` (the id of the chosen concept).\\n\\n1. /Users/me/Obsidian/01-projects/medical-trust-center/mockup/03-story-and-pages.md (\`type: mockup-plan\`):\\n   - **Story** — the demo in one sentence.\\n   - **Steps** — 6 to 12 numbered steps, as the presenter clicks through them. Mark exactly ONE as the step that sells it, the one the brief and the concept point at. Never several.\\n   - **Pages** — each page (a Next.js route by default; a PWA only if the brief asks for one) with the steps it serves, by number.\\n2. /Users/me/Obsidian/01-projects/medical-trust-center/mockup/04-data.md (\`type: mockup-data\`): the cast (the invented people or things the demo shows, with names), the scenario (what happened before the demo starts), and the quantities in a table. All invented, never real.\\n3. /Users/me/Obsidian/01-projects/medical-trust-center/mockup/05-visual-direction.md (\`type: mockup-directions\`, and \`options: [a, b]\` with the ids on one line): 2 or 3 directions, each under \`## <id> — <title>\`, with:\\n   - its tokens: colours (with their values), type, spacing, radius;\\n   - the contrast of every text and background pair, checked: 4.5:1 or more for body text;\\n   - a table \`| Step | Animation | What it causes |\`. Every row names a step of 03-story-and-pages.md by its number and name: an animation that serves no step does not go in.\\n\\n## The directions, as pages\\n\\nIn /Users/me/BWR/Projects/MedicalTrustCenter/directions/ make a static site, plain HTML, CSS and JavaScript, no build step and nothing to install:\\n\\n- \`index.html\`, linking to each direction;\\n- one page per direction, \`<id>.html\`, that shows THE STEP THAT SELLS IT in that direction, with its animations running. It must work on a phone (390 px wide) and respect \`prefers-reduced-motion\`.\\n\\nThe data on the pages comes from 04-data.md. Do not touch \`_versions/\` in that folder.\\n\\n## Publishing\\n\\nPublish /Users/me/BWR/Projects/MedicalTrustCenter/directions to a Vercel preview, from inside that folder:\\n\\n1. \`vercel project add medical-trust-center-directions\` — an answer that it already exists is fine.\\n2. \`vercel link --yes --project medical-trust-center-directions\`\\n3. \`vercel deploy --yes\` — a preview, never \`--prod\`. It prints the deployment URL (https://….vercel.app).\\n4. \`vercel project protection disable medical-trust-center-directions --sso\` — a new Vercel project is born protected and its previews ask for a login; the owner opens them on the phone without one.\\n5. \`curl -s -o /dev/null -w \\"%{http_code}\\" <url>\` on every URL you will hand in, until each answers 200. It takes a few seconds after step 4; keep trying for up to two minutes. Never hand in a URL that does not answer 200.\\n\\nIf \`vercel\` fails (not logged in, no network, a quota) or a URL never answers 200, do NOT call \`submit_stage\`: say in your reply what failed, with the command and its error, and end your turn. The owner retries the stage.\\n\\n## Handing it in\\n\\nPass \`options\` to \`submit_stage\`: one per direction, with the same \`id\` and \`title\` as in 05-visual-direction.md, a one-sentence \`blurb\`, and \`url\` = the deployment URL followed by \`/<id>.html\`. 2 or 3 options.\\n\\n## When you are done\\n\\nCall the tool \`submit_stage\` with runId \`0192f3a4-5b6c-7d8e-9f01-23456789abcd\`, files [\\"03-story-and-pages.md\\",\\"04-data.md\\",\\"05-visual-direction.md\\"] and a one-sentence summary. If it refuses, fix what it says and call it again. When it accepts, end your turn: the owner reviews it from the phone."
`;
